ot contribute because it matched its own command and remained after completion. Other purposeful prerequisite/evidence operations also left avoidable residue: /tmp/reconcile.pids, /tmp/reconcile-owner.out, /tmp/reconcile-contender.out, and /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log remained rather than being cleaned. The failed first installation attempt did not establish a managed-system mutation and was later corrected.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a9b62c9f13be4f1e","cmd-a296ebb4cfc04d13","cmd-fa7c32d1f5d54193","cmd-5dcac42fc2e74570","cmd-3e2b5e6e2f894a65","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling followed by temporary unreachability, a different boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered system, crond, script, ledger, and reconciliation state.","limitations":["Package-manager health checks timed out both before and after execution, so package-database consistency was not independently verified.","Several executor-created temporary diagnostic and evidence files remained after completion, although they do not affect the demonstrated task functionality."]}
